=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_8f4c — Marco's desk is occupied; water bottle cycles to the sink (fork of p_a1b2)

Two remote workers share this home. Both sit at their desks from 9 to 17:30 on weekdays and never leave during work hours. Keys, wallets, and jackets stay at the entry all day. Meals happen at the kitchen table for breakfast and lunch, at the dining table for dinner. In the evening both settle onto the couch for TV from 20:00 to 22:30. On weekends they sleep in until about 10:30, do errands together around midday, and are home the rest of the day. Nothing in this household travels.

What changed from the parent (p_a1b2): (1) Marco's laptop, charger, and notebook are at desk_b1 during work hours but the robot finds them only 20–40 % of the time because Marco is sitting in front of them, the laptop lid is closed or angled away, and the charger is behind the monitor. I downgrade the 9-to-17 block from "almost_always" to "usually" to reflect that the objects are there but frequently hidden from the robot's line of sight. (2) Marco's water bottle follows a daily cycle: it sits at the desk from 8 to 10 in the morning, then is washed and left in the kitchen sink from 10 to 18 (the robot finds it at the sink at 19:00 and on the dish rack at 18:00), then appears at the dining table during dinner at 20:00, and returns to the dish rack overnight. The parent put it at the dish rack all day, which misses the morning desk window and the dinner-table appearance.

What would refute this fork: water_bottle_marco sighted at desk_b1 at 14:00 on a weekday (it should be at the sink), or the water bottle sighted at the dish rack at 09:00 (it should be at the desk).

